=== 1b. Field-independent transitions (clock points) from the Breit-Rabi formula ===
43Ca+ |4,0>-|3,+1>: B0 = 146.0942 G, f0 = 3,199,941,076.93 Hz, d2f/dB2 = 0.002 Hz/mG^2 -> 2.415 mHz/mG^2   [Harty: 146.094 G, 3,199,941,077 Hz, 2.4 mHz/mG^2]
9Be+  |2,0>-|1,+1>: B0 = 119.446 G, f0 = 1,207,495,853.5 Hz, d2f/dB2 = 6.097 mHz/mG^2   [Langer 2005: 119.45 G, ~1,207,495,843 Hz]
25Mg+ |3,1>-|2,+1>: B0 = 212.78 G, f0 = 1,686,462,050 Hz, d2f/dB2 = 4.656 mHz/mG^2   [Srinivas 2021: 212.8 G, ~1.686 GHz]
171Yb+ clock quadratic shift: numeric 310.85 Hz/G^2, closed form (gJ-gI)^2 mu_B^2/(2 h A) = 310.85 Hz/G^2   [Fisk/Olmschenk: 310.8 Hz/G^2]
133Ba+ clock quadratic shift, closed form ignoring gI: 395.7 Hz/G^2

=== 2. Wigner-Eckart hyperfine line strengths (Steck convention) ===
171Yb+ S1/2(F) -> P1/2(F') summed strengths S_FF' (normalized so that sum over F' for fixed F equals 1):
   F=0 -> F'=0: 0.000000
   F=0 -> F'=1: 1.000000
   F=1 -> F'=0: 0.333333
   F=1 -> F'=1: 0.666667
   decay branching P1/2 F'=0: -> F=0 0.0000, -> F=1 1.0000   [expected F'=0 -> F=1 only (=1.0); F'=1 -> 1/3 F=0, 2/3 F=1]
   decay branching P1/2 F'=1: -> F=0 0.3333, -> F=1 0.6667   [expected F'=0 -> F=1 only (=1.0); F'=1 -> 1/3 F=0, 2/3 F=1]
   I=1/2 S1/2|1,1> -> P3/2: cycling |2,2> share of total absorption strength = 0.5000  [expect 1/2 with this sum over all q; sigma+ only: 1.0]

